{"description":"Persist steward loop checkpoints (step, selected driver, worker outputs, EKA writes applied) so a crashed or killed steward resumes deterministically without duplicating EKA writes or re-dispatching completed work. EKA writes supplied by steward carry deterministic instance-versions (auto `max+1` forbidden); on resume, reconcile intent-\u003eresult by reading the line's newest instance digest vs the checkpoint digest; a re-issued write is a same-form, idempotent `PutUnit` no-op. Checkpoint storage location is defined (outside EKA) and written atomically (temp+fsync+rename).","acceptanceCriteria":"Killing steward mid-loop and restarting resumes from the last checkpoint.\nNo EKA write is applied twice (resume reconciles by line digest; same-form re-issue is a no-op).\nCompleted work is not re-dispatched.\nCheckpoint storage location is defined and written atomically; the format is versioned and tested."}